\section{Saved-result reuse}{

The returned \code{fit_identity} records the fitted analysis for reuse with
reports and exports. Recreate older results from the saved fit and matching
diagnostics using the original screening options; no model refit is needed.
See \link{mfrmr_compatibility_layer} for migration instructions.
}

\section{Controls}{

For \code{plot()}:
\itemize{
\item \code{facet_a}, \code{facet_b}, or \code{interaction_facets} identify the interaction;
\code{top_n = 40} and \code{sort_by = "abs_t"} (\code{"abs_bias"} or \code{"prob"} also
accepted) select ranked interactions.
\item \code{abs_t_warn = 2}, \code{abs_bias_warn = 0.5}, and \code{p_max = 0.05} set
screening rules when preparing a report from the bias result. They are
review aids, not guarantees of a calibrated error rate.
\item \code{show_ci = FALSE} omits whiskers; \code{ci_level = 0.95} chooses their level
for scatter/ranked views. GPCM rows retain conditional profile bounds,
with dashed whiskers for search-limited or unverified bounds. Other rows
use conditional per-cell SEs. Missing profile bounds are not replaced
with another method. These intervals omit calibration uncertainty;
endpoint completion is not evidence of coverage.
\item \code{preset} selects \code{"standard"}, \code{"publication"}, \code{"compact"}, or
\code{"monochrome"}; \code{palette} overrides named colors (\code{normal}, \code{flag},
\code{hist}, \code{profile}); \code{label_angle} controls label rotation. \code{title} sets
title metadata (\code{main} is a compatibility alias; supply only one).
}
}

\section{Plot types}{

\describe{
\item{\code{"scatter"} (default)}{Observed-minus-expected score average (x)
versus conditional bias size in logits (y). Points use the saved flag
status; horizontal guides show the saved absolute-bias threshold and
zero, with a vertical guide at zero score difference.}
\item{\code{"ranked"}}{Conditional bias size (x) for up to \code{top_n} saved
ranked interactions (y). Points are colored by flag status; optional
whiskers retain the conditional uncertainty and incomplete-bound status.
A saved report retains the ranking chosen when it was constructed.}
\item{\code{"heatmap"}}{Facet A by facet B matrix of signed bias size.
Cells retain reusable matrix and flag tables for dashboards. This is
a Table 13 follow-up display: it supports pattern recognition but does
not turn screening rows into confirmatory tests.}
\item{\code{"abs_t_hist"}}{Histogram of absolute screening t-statistics across all
interaction cells.  Dashed reference line at \code{abs_t_warn}.  Use for
assessing the overall distribution of interaction effect sizes.}
\item{\code{"facet_profile"}}{Per-facet-level aggregation showing mean
absolute bias and flag rate.  Useful for identifying which
individual facet levels drive systematic interaction patterns.}
}
}

